close your eyes and think of the worst  movie you saw in 2021 got it good now  forget it because we can pretty much  guarantee that these were a whole lot  worse  from the exorcist to the devils to the  omen the 1970s were undoubtedly a golden  age for religious horror movies there  have been a few standout additions to  the subgenre since but most contemporary  faith-based horrors failed to capture  the haunting magic of the apomentic  classics and 2021 zion holy is a prime  example it's the story of a  hearing-impaired girl named alice who  after a visit from the virgin mary finds  that she has gained the ability to heal  the sick what could possibly go wrong  i slit their windpipes and watch the  breath slowly leak out  as it turns out a lot to put a long  story short the unholy is a tale of  witchcraft deception creepy dolls and uh  journalism disgraced reporter gary fenn  accidentally released the spirit of a  witch who then possessed alice under the  guise of the virgin mary naturally it's  up to him to save her from the clutches  of the aforementioned grumpy crone  cricket brown and jeffrey dean morgan do  their utmost to elevate the cliche  written script but the by the numbers  plot predictable jump scares and  substandard special effects make the  unholy a genuinely unenjoyable  experience perhaps unsurprisingly the  majority of critics had nothing but bad  things to say about this unholy misfire  based on the real-life crimes of the  truck stop killer midnight in the  switchgrass follows two fbi agents carl  helter and his partner rebecca lombardi  who are hunting a serial killer at work  in florida's underworld when lombardi is  kidnapped by the man thereafter helter  teams up with a state level cop to get  her back and catch the killer despite  featuring prominently in the promotional  material bruce willis appears in  precious few scenes in this movie as is  pretty much the norm of these films  nowadays modern willis movies also tend  to get a real hammering from the critics  and midnight in the switch grass is no  exception as the new york times review  said the atmosphere is thoroughly sleazy  without being distinctive and everything  about the movie the emotionless line  readings the half-baked backstories  exudes a terse functionality when the  dust had settled this thoroughly lazy  thriller was left with a damning score  of just eight percent from critics on  rotten tomatoes the only people who  might gain something from midnight in  the switchgrass are fans of megan fox  and machine gun kelly their relationship  began on the set of the movie but even  they're under no illusions about its  quality the couple pulled out of the  premiere and kelly appeared to call the  film trash in a tweet days later by all  rights naked singularity should have  been one of the best movies of 2021  produced by ridley scott and featuring  the likes of olivia cook and john boyega  this unconventional comedy drama had all  the makings of a modern classic while  yega stars is a new york city public  defender going through a moral crisis  after learning that a client is involved  in a 50 million dollar drug deal he  decides to steal the money from right  under their nose there are plenty of  good ideas here but sloppy execution  lets naked singularity down threads that  were fully fleshed out and sergio de la  pava's original novel go nowhere here  and writer director chase palmer doesn't  seem to know what genre his adaptation  belongs to as the new york times puts it  naked singularity welds legal drama and  science fiction into a misshapen crime  caper  when a film has a zero percent rating on  rotten tomatoes a month on from its  release it's usually safe to say that  it's not going to be remembered as a  classic inhabit the debut feature from  writer director janelle shurtcliff  probably won't be remembered by anyone  but die hard fans of bella thorne the  former disney channel actor stars as a  los angeles socialite who pays the bills  by selling drugs for a washed up  hollywood star when a drug deal goes  sour and some cash is stolen she and her  hard partying pals go on the run dressed  as nuns for some reason it really does  seem like shirt cliff woke up one day  and decided that a bunch of la girls  beating the hell out of a guy while  dressed as nuns would look cool on  camera and then proceeded to build an  entire movie around that idea there was  some backlash to the film when it was  announced mostly to do with the casting  of paris jackson as jesus but the final  product is more of a crime against  cinema than anything else abbott tries  so very hard to be edgy so much so that  the movie's press release actually  described it as being reminiscent of  early tarantino the truth is  you're the weak  and i am the tyranny of evil men  but the plot is paper thin and there's  next to nothing in terms of character  development variety definitely summed up  this mercifully short film of the single  sentence in its review calling it a  candy colored dress-up excuse for a  bunch of slumming models rock musicians  and miscellaneous scenesters  where did it all go wrong for neil  blumkamp at one stage the south african  director was in line to take charge of a  new alien movie but his stock has fallen  significantly in recent years in an  interview with the guardian blumkant  recently joked it's possible that ridley  scott watched chappie and he was like  this guy can't do aliens so let's just  go ahead and move on he was speaking to  the british newspaper to promote his  2021 supernatural horror flick demonic  which unfortunately for blumkamp got  panned even worse than his much derided  2015 sci-fi flick champion demonic are  beset by similar issues they're just a  lot more apparent in the latter filmed  during the covet 19 pandemic demonic is  a far more contained movie and therefore  can't always hide behind its vfx it  follows a young woman who gets the  chance to go inside the mind of her  comatose serial killer mother via new  technology when she enters the  simulation however she finds a demon and  it turns out that her mother was  possessed and that the whole experiment  is being overseen by a vatican black ops  unit if this all sounds a little out  there that's because it is what's worse  is that the director seems unwilling to  fully commit to the bonkers premise as  brian talarico of roger ebert.com put it  demonic feels like a film made by  someone who's scared of his own ideas  and his own limitations  people who saw romeo must die back in  2000 probably thought they'd never see  the day that an even worse contemporary  retelling of romeo and juliet could hit  cineplexes but on july 16 2021 that's  exactly what happened die in a gunfight  stars diego banetta and alexandra  daddario as romeo and juliet or actually  ben and mary two star-crossed lovers  from powerful families that have been at  war since the 1860s their families are  determined to keep them apart but as  you've almost certainly figured out by  now they disregard the long-running feud  and follow their hearts instead viking  star travis fimmel also shows up as a  typically intense hitman and the film is  narrated by billy crudup for some reason  upon seeing it it becomes clear why this  movie spent over a decade in development  hell zac efron was all set to star in  and produce diana gunfight in 2010  variety later claimed that josh  hutcherson and kya scodelario had agreed  to play ben and mary but that also fell  through would any of these actors have  been able to save the movie bonnetta and  daddario don't exactly shine though  their characters are so thinly written  that it's little wonder so many actors  passed on the project beforehand they  certainly weren't helped by director  colin shifley who opts for action movie  cliches and excessive neon lighting over  any meaningful exploration of the  protagonist's characters  if you've already forgotten about the  2019 animated feature of the adams  family you're not alone despite boasting  an impressive voice cast including oscar  isaac and charlize theron as gomez and  morticia the kid-friendly reboot of this  classic property wasn't exactly a hit  with the critics though low production  costs meant it was still able to turn a  healthy profit a second film was  announced pretty much immediately and  the a-list voice cast all signed on to  reprise their roles unfortunately their  combined talents were not enough to save  this flat and equally forgettable  follow-up the addams family too is the  kind of film that could only be enjoyed  by an atoms because it's torture this  painfully unfunny sequel follows the  titular family on a camper van trip  organized by gomez who fears the adam's  clan isn't as tight-knit as it once was  detective pikachu scribes dan hernandez  and benji sammit were among the numerous  writers who contributed to the script  which is nevertheless paper-thin  extremely light on laughs and nowhere  near kooky enough for long-time adam's  family fans  empire magazine said of the film  ironically given the mantra for its main  characters is about embracing the weird  the adams family too does little that is  out there or different delivering a safe  stale 93 minutes  the halloween franchise got a fresh  start in 2018 when a brand new  installment blew up the box office and  scored rave reviews this new halloween  ignored all the films that had followed  1978's halloween and continued the story  of lori strode decades later the critics  loved it too the same cannot be said of  2021's halloween kills the shockingly  bland second entry in a planned sequel  trilogy halloween kills begins  immediately after the conclusion of the  previous film in which lori locked  escaped killer michael myers in the  basement of her house and set it ablaze  it soon becomes clear that responding  firefighters released him and he's  coming for lori once again but here's  what seemed to annoy people towards the  end of the movie myers is set upon by an  angry mob taking a beating that no  mortal man could survive yet he does  after being shot and stabbed multiple  times michael gets up and proceeds to  slaughter the now terrified townsfolk  this ending caused confusion and  disappointment in equal measure  seemingly confirming that michael myers  draws power from supernatural sources  previous halloween sequels have taken  this path and the original did actually  hint at it  i killed him  he can't kill the boogeyman  but nobody expected this movie to follow  suit making michael truly immortal was a  major cop-out that only served to set up  the final installment as such halloween  kills is a pointless stepping stone of a  movie doing nothing to advance the  overarching story and failing to deliver  any real scares either  sometimes something that works perfectly  on stage just doesn't make the same  impact on screen this is certainly the  case with dear evan hansen the story of  a high school loner who gets swept up in  a lie after a classmate dies by suicide  on the advice of his therapist evan  writes letters to himself some of which  mention his crush zoe connor zoe's  brother snatches one of his letters  before taking his own life which leads  everyone to assume the letter is conor's  last missive to evan instead of coming  clean evan manufactures a fake  friendship between him and conor putting  his parents minds at ease and allowing  him to get closer to zoe it's not easy  to get behind a character who would do  such a thing though ben platt made it  possible on broadway he reprises the  title role in the 2021 film adaptation  which keeps the tunes but lacks the  offbeat charm without an audience to  beat off of platt's performance falls  flat as far as the music is concerned  the songs don't have the same impact as  they did on stage as the chicago sun  times review pointed out upbeat tunes  and a heavy storyline about teen suicide  make a cringy combo  if you or anyone you know is having  suicidal thoughts please call the  national suicide prevention lifeline at  1-800-273-talk 8255

